# Examples Directory

This directory contains comprehensive examples and tutorials for using NLM (Neural Learning Machine). Examples range from simple "Hello World" to advanced multi-agent systems.

## Overview

NLM examples cover:
- Basic brain creation and usage
- Complete simulation workflows
- Learning and development examples
- Multi-agent systems
- Advanced features for experienced users
- Performance optimization techniques

## Usage

Most examples follow this pattern:

```python
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Example: [Title]"""

import pynlm

def main():
    # Setup
    config = pynlm.createDefaultConfig()
    brain = pynlm.createBrain(config)
    brain.initialize()
    
    world = pynlm.createSimpleWorld()
    world.configure(width=20, height=20, visionWidth=8, visionHeight=8)
    world.reset()
    
    agent = pynlm.createAgentBrain(brain)
    agent.initialize(world)
    
    # Enable learning for advanced examples
    agent.enableRewardModulation(True)
    agent.enableCuriosity(True)
    agent.enableDevelopment(True)
    
    # Run simulation
    for step in range(200):
        world.update(0.1)
        agent.processSensoryInput(world.getSensoryPercept())
        brain.step(step)
        action = agent.decodeMotorCommand()
        world.applyMotorCommand(action, world.getSimulationTime())
    
    # Analyze results
    print(f"Simulation completed with {brain.getFiringNeuronCount()} neurons firing")
    print(f"Development stage: {brain.getDevelopmentalStage().name}")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```

